{
  "info": {
    "name": "ABDM HIE-CM Gateway session",
    "description": "Generated from the ABDM HIE-CM specifications. Import hiecm-sandbox.postman_environment.json beside it and fill in clientId and clientSecret: the collection fetches a gateway session token before a call when it needs one.\n\nFolders follow the order a journey is built in. Send the steps in order: each response keeps the txnId and the X-token it returns as collection variables, and the steps after it read them. Callbacks are not included: ABDM sends those to your bridge URL, so receiving them needs a public endpoint, not Postman.\n\nValues ABDM expects encrypted, such as an Aadhaar number or an OTP, are shown as the specification gives them. Encrypt your own values before sending.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Gets a gateway session token when there is none or it has expired.",
          "(function () {",
          "if (pm.request.url.getPath().endsWith('/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/sessions')) return;",
          "const expiry = Number(pm.environment.get('accessTokenExpiry') || 0);",
          "if (pm.environment.get('accessToken') && Date.now() < expiry) return;",
          "pm.sendRequest({",
          "  url: pm.variables.replaceIn('{{gatewayUrl}}/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/sessions'),",
          "  method: 'POST',",
          "  header: {",
          "    'Content-Type': 'application/json',",
          "    'REQUEST-ID': pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'),",
          "    'TIMESTAMP': new Date().toISOString(),",
          "    'X-CM-ID': pm.variables.replaceIn('{{cmId}}'),",
          "  },",
          "  body: {",
          "    mode: 'raw',",
          "    raw: JSON.stringify({",
          "      clientId: pm.variables.get('clientId'),",
          "      clientSecret: pm.variables.get('clientSecret'),",
          "      grantType: 'client_credentials',",
          "    }),",
          "  },",
          "}, (error, response) => {",
          "  if (error || response.code >= 300) {",
          "    console.error('Session token request failed', error || response.text());",
          "    return;",
          "  }",
          "  const {accessToken, expiresIn} = response.json();",
          "  pm.environment.set('accessToken', accessToken);",
          "  // A minute early, so a token never expires between this check and the call.",
          "  pm.environment.set('accessTokenExpiry', Date.now() + (expiresIn - 60) * 1000);",
          "});",
          "})();"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keeps what this response hands to the calls after it, such as the txnId an",
          "// OTP request returns and the X-token a login returns, as collection variables.",
          "(function () {",
          "let body;",
          "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (error) { return; }",
          "function carriedValues(body) {",
          "  const list = Array.isArray(body);",
          "  const first = list ? body[0] : body;",
          "  if (!first || typeof first !== \"object\") return {};",
          "  const read = (path) => {",
          "    let at = first;",
          "    for (const key of path.split(\".\")) {",
          "      if (!at || typeof at !== \"object\") return void 0;",
          "      at = at[key];",
          "    }",
          "    return typeof at === \"string\" && at ? at : void 0;",
          "  };",
          "  const out = {};",
          "  const txnId = read(\"txnId\");",
          "  if (txnId) out[list ? \"searchTxnId\" : \"txnId\"] = txnId;",
          "  const tokenAt = [\"tokens.token\", \"jwtResponse.token\", \"token\"].find((path) => read(path));",
          "  if (tokenAt) {",
          "    const token = read(tokenAt);",
          "    out[\"X-token\"] = token;",
          "    out.jwtToken = token;",
          "    const refresh = read(tokenAt.replace(/token$/, \"refreshToken\"));",
          "    if (refresh) out[\"R-jwtToken\"] = refresh;",
          "  }",
          "  return out;",
          "}",
          "const values = carriedValues(body);",
          "Object.keys(values).forEach(function (key) { pm.collectionVariables.set(key, values[key]); });",
          "})();"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "txnId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "searchTxnId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "X-token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "jwtToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "R-jwtToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Bridge",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Fetch the service ids registered against a bridge",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "REQUEST-ID",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-CM-ID",
                "value": "{{cmId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/bridge-services",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "hiecm",
                "gateway",
                "v3",
                "bridge-services"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve the unique identifiers, known as service IDs, that are associated with a specific bridge. In this context, a bridge acts as an intermediary component that connects various services or networks, enabling them to communicate with each other. When you call this API, it queries the bridge to gather a list of all the service IDs that have been registered with it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Fetch the details of a service ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "REQUEST-ID",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-CM-ID",
                "value": "{{cmId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/bridge-service/serviceId/:service-id",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "hiecm",
                "gateway",
                "v3",
                "bridge-service",
                "serviceId",
                ":service-id"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "service-id",
                  "value": ""
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve the details associated with a specific service ID. When invoked, it queries the system to fetch comprehensive information about the service identified by the provided service ID."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Update the bridge URL",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "REQUEST-ID",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-CM-ID",
                "value": "{{cmId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/bridge/url",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "hiecm",
                "gateway",
                "v3",
                "bridge",
                "url"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"<YOUR_CALLBACK_URL>\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Update the URL of a bridge. When invoked, it allows users to modify the existing URL associated with a specific bridge. This functionality is crucial for maintaining accurate and up-to-date connection information within the network. By using this API, administrators can ensure that the bridge URL reflects the current configuration and routing requirements, facilitating seamless communication and integration between different services in the form of webhook site."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Session",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Generate access token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "REQUEST-ID",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-CM-ID",
                "value": "{{cmId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/sessions",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "hiecm",
                "gateway",
                "v3",
                "sessions"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"SBX_0000\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"0******-***-***-***-a****\",\n  \"grantType\": \"client_credentials\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Generate an access token. When invoked, it facilitates the authentication process by providing a secure token that can be used to access various services and resources within the system. This functionality is essential for ensuring secure and authorised access, enabling users to interact with protected endpoints and perform operations that require authentication. By using this API, users can obtain the necessary tokens to maintain secure sessions and access the system’s features effectively."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
